  "en": {
    "cover": {
      "kicker": "Review signals",
      "headline": "Buyer GT-NIT:2342855 concentrates awards via direct purchase",
      "dek": "An aggregate pattern of 18,931 contracts and a Q1,592,430.37 single-bidder award trigger contracts worth reviewing."
    },
    "theCase": "The buyer identified as GT-NIT:2342855 accumulates 18,931 contracts flagged by the direct-award overreliance rule during the review period. Aggregated case data indicates a direct value-share of 0.9899 across 13,028 awards totaling Q712,649,385.80 in direct value (ev:0, ev:1). In parallel, 390 contracts are recorded with a single bidder, summing Q38,826,410.56, with a top representative award of Q1,592,430.37 (ev:63064). These are unusual patterns versus comparable contracts and form part of the contracts worth reviewing.",
    "followTheMoney": "The highest representative amount in the single-bidder sample reaches Q1,592,430.37 (ev:63064), followed by Q1,102,058 (ev:63240), Q348,226.98 (ev:63066), Q245,426.46 (ev:63046), Q245,162.46 (ev:63592) and Q241,031.04 (ev:63048). The aggregate case reports Q38,826,410.56 summed under the single-bidder rule and Q712,649,385.80 in buyer direct value (ev:1). By signal count, the most frequent suppliers are GT-NIT:22345388 (1,441), GT-NIT:7477279 (855), GT-NIT:94197016 (454), GT-NIT:735442 (318) and GT-NIT:5801338 (309).",
    "theConnections": "Concentration appears both by method and by supplier recurrence. The overreliance rule flags methods including Compra Directa con Oferta Electrónica (Art. 43 LCE Inciso b) (ev:0), Cotización (Art. 38 LCE) (ev:2) and Licitación Pública (Art. 17 LCE) (ev:4) under the same buyer. In addition, 12,469 contracts were flagged by the failed-then-single-award rule, with representative re-awards to GT-NIT:120443058 for Q4,800 (ev:37863) and to GT-NIT:3014290 for Q89,680 (ev:37865).",
    "timeline": "The case digest does not provide a consolidated date range for the scope window scope:2026-04..2026-05. Available temporal references correspond to prior OCIDs tied to processes recorded as Desierto on 2026-04-07 (ev:37862) and Prescindido on 2026-04-06 (ev:37864, ev:37866), each followed by single-supplier re-awards within the 90-day window defined by the rule.",
    "closing": {
      "whatItMeans": "The aggregate counts — 18,931 contracts under direct-award overreliance, 12,469 under failed-then-single-award, 390 under single bidder and 163 under low competition vs category — constitute signals to prioritize documentary review of buyer GT-NIT:2342855. They do not establish legal responsibility on the part of any party.",
      "caveat": "These are review signals, not conclusions of illegality."
    },
    "keyFindings": [
      "18,931 contracts flagged for direct-award overreliance under buyer GT-NIT:2342855 (ev:0, ev:1).",
      "Direct value-share of 0.9899 across 13,028 awards and Q712,649,385.80 in total direct value (ev:1).",
      "390 single-bidder contracts sum Q38,826,410.56, with top representative award of Q1,592,430.37 (ev:63064).",
      "12,469 contracts flagged for failed-then-single-award patterns (ev:37862–ev:37867).",
      "163 contracts with bidder counts below their category-family p25 (ev:62800–ev:62805)."
    ]
  },
